config BR2_PACKAGE_GARGOYLE_TIMERANGE
	bool "gargoyle-timerange"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	select BR2_PACKAGE_IPTABLES
	help
	  Gargoyle xt_timerange netfilter match.

	  Builds the libxt_timerange.so iptables/ip6tables extension and
	  enables CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TIMERANGE, so the xt_timerange module
	  (patched into the kernel by 0008-xt-timerange.patch) is built too.

	  The match tests packets against hours-of-day, days-of-week and
	  weekly time ranges; it is used by Gargoyle to make bandwidth quotas
	  active only during chosen on-peak / off-peak windows.

	  Originally from Gargoyle router firmware (gargoyle-router.com).

comment "gargoyle-timerange needs a Linux kernel to be built"
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
